#Core
	- Domain(Class Library)
		- Core of the system 
		- Has Domain Entity, Business Role, Aggregate, Value Object , Domain Events (Domain Driven Design), IUnitOfWork, IRepository, Factory Interfaces , Domain Services , Custom Exceptions 
		- Domain should be an independent project.
		- All Other layers can access domain layer but not oppposite
		- Packages
			- Microsoft.AspNetCore.Identity.EntityFrameworkCore
			- Microsoft.AspNetCore.Identity.UI
	- Application(Class Library)
		- should depend on Domain.
		- Has Use Cases, Application Services , Commands and Queries (CQRS pattern)
		- packages
			- Install-Package MediatR
			- Install-Package FluentValidation.DependencyInjectionExtension
#External
	- Infrastructure(Class Library)
		- should depend on Application and Domain.
		- Anything is related to external systems 
		- Hiding The implementation details for any External system to interact with it
		- Has Databases Access, Messages Queues (RabbitMQ, Kafka), Email & Notification Service, Storage Service
		- split into two seperate layers 
		- persistance layer that we would handle anything related to database access
		- Infrastructure layer would handle other external systems like email notifcation message Queues, Storage Service
		- Add ApplicationDbContext
		- Add Implementation of IUnitOfWork, IRepository
		- packages
			- Install-Package Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection
			- Install-Package Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore
			- Install-Package Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.SqlServer
			- Install-Package Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.JwtBearer
			- Install-Package System.IdentityModel.Tokens.Jwt
			- Install-Package AutoMapper
	- Presentation(Class Library) WebApi
		- should depend on Infrastructure and Application.
		- Define the entry point for outer users to be able to interact with system 
		- Implemented Restful Api, grpc
		- packages
			- Install-Package Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection
			- Install-Package Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.NewtonsoftJson
		- Add Controllers
WebApi(Web API)
	- instead of define controller in web api layer, we define in presentation layer because if 
		we define all controllers in web layer, we reference all other layers in web layer, and then we can access dbcontext in web layer and its break using the CQRS pattern
		so we define all controllers in presentation layer 
	- Add Middlewares
	- packages
		- Install-Package Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore
		- Install-Package Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.SqlServer
		- Install-Package Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Tools

#How to start
	- In Domain layer 
		- In Entities folder Add Domain Entity
		- In Abstractions/IUnitOfWork Add Repository 
	- In Infrastructure layer 
		- In ApplicationDbContext.cs Add DbSet<Entity>
		- In Repositories/UnitOfWork Implement IUnitOfWork
		- Add migration, update database using Package Manager Console
	- In Application layer
		- in DTOs create dto for entity
		- create commands and queries for this entity
		- mapping profile
		- in Extensions/DependencyInjection in MapperConfiguration add mapping profile
	- Presentation layer
		- 


